## Important Constraints

1. **Never start coding without a plan** for tasks touching more than one logical change.
2. **Add only the logs runtime verification needs.** Log what proves the feature executed and produced the right result — not a mechanical entry/exit on every method. A simple delegation or getter needs no log. An external call, a branching decision, or a computed result does.
3. **Only new code gets the feature tag.** `feature:<tag>` in VictoriaLogs must only appear in code written for this task — that keeps the query unambiguous. Never add the tag to pre-existing methods.
4. **Never move to the next sub-task** while the current one has any failing static or runtime gate.
5. **Never use INFO for per-request paths.** Always DEBUG for operations that run on every request.
6. **Never log sensitive data** — no API keys, tokens, passwords, or PII in any log line.
7. **Never skip runtime verification** because "the build passed." Runtime behavior must be verified via Docker + VictoriaLogs + APIs.
8. **Plan doc is a living document** — update sub-task status after every validation pass, not at the end.
9. **Feature tag per sub-task**, not one per whole task — it keeps VictoriaLogs queries focused on exactly the code being validated right now.
10. **Never add an external call without metrics, error logging, and a circuit breaker.** Silent external failures cause cascading production incidents.
11. **Never put imports anywhere except the top of the file.** Inline imports are only acceptable for documented circular dependency workarounds.

---

## When This Rule Does NOT Apply

- Pure documentation edits
- Read-only code exploration or questions
- Variable/method renames with zero logic change
- Comment-only or formatting-only edits
